            Enter the world between the words
        </div>

        <h1>
            Poetry<br>
            <em>Speaks</em> Louder
        </h1>

        <p class="hero-description">
            Some feelings are too deep for ordinary language.
            So we give them metaphors, give them silence,
            and sometimes give them a universe of their own.
        </p>

        <a href="#poetry" class="enter">
            ENTER THE POETIC WORLD
        </a>

    </div>

</section>


<!-- POETRY WORLD -->
<section class="poetry-world" id="poetry">

    <div class="section-heading">

        <div class="small-title">
            The world between the lines
        </div>

        <h2>Where Words Become Worlds</h2>

        <p>MOVE YOUR EYES. LET THE POEMS MOVE YOU.</p>

    </div>


    <div class="poem-slider">

        <div class="poem-track">


            <!-- POEM 01 -->
            <article class="poem">

                <div class="poem-number">01 / THE FIRST DOOR</div>

                <h3>The Moon Forgot Me</h3>

                <p>
                    Last night, the moon forgot my name.
                    <br><br>
                    So I wrote it on the ocean,
                    and watched the waves erase me
                    one letter at a time.
                    <br><br>
                    Perhaps that is what becoming is—
                    <em>learning to exist after the world
                    has stopped remembering you.</em>
                </p>

                <div class="author">POETRY SPEAKS LOUDER</div>

            </article>


            <!-- POEM 02 -->
            <article class="poem">

                <div class="poem-number">02 / THE SECOND DOOR</div>

                <h3>She Was A Sunrise</h3>

                <p>
                    She did not enter my life like a person.
                    <br><br>
                    She arrived like morning—
                    quietly convincing the darkness
                    that it had somewhere else to be.
                    <br><br>
                    And suddenly,
                    even my shadows began
                    <em>learning how to bloom.</em>
                </p>

                <div class="author">POETRY SPEAKS LOUDER</div>

            </article>


            <!-- POEM 03 -->
            <article class="poem">

                <div class="poem-number">03 / THE THIRD DOOR</div>

                <h3>My Heart Is A House</h3>

                <p>
                    My heart is a house
                    built beside a forgotten river.
                    <br><br>
                    Every room carries an echo.
                    Every window waits for rain.
                    <br><br>
                    And you—
                    you were not a guest.
                    You were the key
                    <em>that taught the doors
                    why they were made.</em>
                </p>

                <div class="author">POETRY SPEAKS LOUDER</div>

            </article>


            <!-- POEM 04 -->
            <article class="poem">

                <div class="poem-number">04 / THE FOURTH DOOR</div>

                <h3>We Were Two Rivers</h3>

                <p>
                    We were two rivers
                    pretending we had separate destinations.
                    <br><br>
                    We crossed mountains,
                    swallowed stones,
                    survived droughts.
                    <br><br>
                    Until one evening
                    our waters touched
                    and the world called it
                    <em>love.</em>
                </p>

                <div class="author">POETRY SPEAKS LOUDER</div>

            </article>


            <!-- POEM 05 -->
            <article class="poem">

                <div class="poem-number">05 / THE FIFTH DOOR</div>

                <h3>I Planted A Star</h3>

                <p>
                    I buried a star
                    beneath the soil of yesterday.
                    <br><br>
                    Everyone told me
                    stars belong to the sky.
                    <br><br>
                    But I waited.
                    <br><br>
                    And when tomorrow came,
                    <em>you grew.</em>
                </p>

                <div class="author">POETRY SPEAKS LOUDER</div>

            </article>


            <!-- POEM 06 -->
            <article class="poem">

                <div class="poem-number">06 / THE SIXTH DOOR</div>

                <h3>The Silence Between Us</h3>

                <p>
                    There was a silence between us
                    larger than language.
                    <br><br>
                    I placed my heart inside it
                    like a candle inside a cathedral.
                    <br><br>
                    You said nothing.
                    <br><br>
                    Yet somehow,
                    <em>the silence answered.</em>
                </p>

                <div class="author">POETRY SPEAKS LOUDER</div>

            </article>


            <!-- POEM 07 -->
            <article class="poem">

                <div class="poem-number">07 / THE SEVENTH DOOR</div>

                <h3>Time Sat Beside Us</h3>

                <p>
                    Time sat beside us
                    pretending not to watch.
                    <br><br>
                    Minutes became birds.
                    Hours became clouds.
                    <br><br>
                    And somewhere between your laughter
                    and my unfinished sentence,
                    <em>forever forgot how to leave.</em>
                </p>

                <div class="author">POETRY SPEAKS LOUDER</div>

            </article>


